course: dictionary
lesson: 7927
title: Reader and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A reader is a person who reads. «She is a good reader» means she reads well. A reader can also be a book used to learn to read, with short easy stories, or a machine that reads something.
explain: Use the words around the word to find out which meaning fits. «The e-reader lets me carry a hundred books.» The words e-reader and carry show a machine, not a person. Ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Writers think about their reader. «A cliffhanger ends a chapter at a tense moment, so the reader must read on.» Here reader means the person reading the story, and the writer is trying to keep them turning the pages.
fact: A reader is a person who reads, or who is reading a book, a paper or a story.
fact: An early reader is a book used to learn to read, often with short easy stories.
fact: An e-reader or a card reader is a machine or app that reads something.
fact: «Keen reader» means someone who loves reading and reads often.
fact: Gaming guides, magazines and fact books count as real reading too, and interest is what keeps a reader going.
exercise: «The children loved their new early reader about a dog called Biscuit.» What is an early reader? | A machine that reads cards | *A book used to learn to read, with short easy stories | A person who reads very fast | A newspaper for grown-ups
exercise: «Dad charged his e-reader before the flight.» What is an e-reader? | *A machine or app that reads something | A pen for writing letters | A bag for carrying books | A person who reads on planes
exercise: «She is a keen reader who finishes a book every week.» What does keen reader mean? | *Someone who loves reading and reads often | Someone who reads aloud for money | Someone who reads only in winter | Someone who cannot read at all
test: «The card reader beeped when I tapped my card.» What does reader mean here? | *A machine that reads something | A book for learning to read | A person who reads | A teacher
test: «A cliffhanger ends a chapter at a tense moment, so the reader must read on.» Why must the reader read on? | *Because the story stops at an exciting, tense moment | Because the reader is bored | Because the book is free | Because the chapter is too long to finish
exam: Which phrase describes a person who loves books? | E-reader | Early reader | Card reader | *Keen reader
